Package: dipsim
Type: Package
Title: Interactive Ashenfelter-Dip Simulator for Synthetic and Augmented Synthetic Control
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: person("Andre", "Bonfrer", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "andre.bonfrer@deakin.edu.au")
Description: A standalone Shiny app that simulates panels in which adoption of a
    budgeting feature is triggered by a transitory shock (an Ashenfelter dip),
    runs the budgetsc synthetic-control stage on them with plain synthetic
    control and ridge-augmented synthetic control fitted on the same panel, and
    shows how the bias depends on the estimator, the augmentation penalty,
    baseline length, held-out matching weeks, the number of matched outcomes,
    donor pool size and shock persistence. Built as a starting point for adding
    further remedies.
